						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I want to take a minute to explain jewelry making so all will get the idea of what it takes to get the skill lvl up.  <br />
So far I have four metals...Silver, Electrum, Gold, Platinum.  There are 28 different types of stones.  As the stones progress they obviously become more and more expensive.  They more basic the stone the easier it is thus far to trivialize (meaning I can go on to the next stone)  Currently I am trivialized in silver up to the Opal stone.  The opal stone alone costs at my price 17 pp at a vendor.  I have gone through 10 of these and still haven't trivialized yet.  So for this stone alone I have spent 107pp to get where I am.  The ruby which is the one following the black pearl which I haven't touched yet is 131 pp at a vendor for just ONE.  It will take me at least a stack to move on from there.  Then comes Sapphire, Star ruby...etc each one progressively more exp and harder to trivialize...the time I'm more than willing to put in but thus far haven't been able to move beyond because of lack of cash.  I would like to hear what you have for ideas and suggestions to help with this small dilemma.  Is it raids for loot?  Should we go to areas for a &quot;raid&quot; to farm stones?  Is it a guild bank account where money or jewels are put and distributed to those who need it.  Be creative...but do list some ideas.  Thankies						</td>
